  "notes": [
    "2026-07-25 DFP SVD audit (Debug/SVD/AE302F80F55D5AE_CM55_HE_View.svd): removed `comparator_lp` (was 1).  This part's SVD peripheral list carries CMP0..CMP3 but NO LPCMP, while the E8 SVD (AE822FA0E5597BS0) carries both -- the low-power comparator is a FA0E5597-generation block this part does not have.  Same defect and same fix as E7 in #932; E3/E5 were out of that pass's reach because the DFP ships no Device/soc/ directory for them, only an SVD.  Per the file convention an absent key means zero instances (no SoC JSON sets a peripheral to 0).  Also re-confirmed correct against the same SVD: i2c_lp 1, spi_lp 1, no i3c_lp, i2c 4, spi 4, uart 8, i2s 4, adc_12bit 3, dac_12bit 2, comparator_hs 4, can_fd 1, ethernet 1, usb_2 1, sdio 1, rtc 1.",
    "Datasheet: 187 pages, ADTS0007 v2.8 May 2024.",
    "Variants differ in NPU-HP presence, CAN-FD presence, MRAM size (5.5 MB vs 1.5 MB), and SRAM tier (13.5 / 8.25 / 5.75 / 3.75 MB).",
    "AE302F80F55D5LE is the variant Alp Lab uses on the E1M-AEN301 module SKU.",
    "debug.jlink_flash_device populated for all 4 variants (#1295; it was 6 before #1444 dropped this file's two WLCSP208 rows), sourced from the SEGGER J-Link DLL V9.46 built-in device table via JLINKARM_DEVICE_GetInfo readback of the AlifSemiconductor block -- canonical entry names, not order-code-alias probing (an earlier probe-based pass in the same issue wrongly published order-code spellings that only resolve as SEGGER aliases). E3 is one of three Ensemble subfamilies (E3/E5/E7) whose device names drop the package/grade suffix and use a bare `_HE` string; E6/E8 keep the full order code plus `_M55_HE`. AE302F80F5582AE/LE share one DB entry (`AE302F80F5582_HE`) and AE302F80F55D5AE/LE share another (`AE302F80F55D5_HE`) -- two order codes legitimately resolving to one device-table entry, confirmed by index readback, not a metadata duplication bug."
  ]
